s=\"longitude\">78°50′36″W&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class=\"geo-multi-punct\">&amp;#xfeff; / &amp;#xfeff;&lt;/span>&lt;span class=\"geo-nondefault\">&lt;span class=\"geo-dec\" title=\"Maps, aerial photos, and other data for this location\">33.72972°N 78.84333°W&lt;/span>&lt;span style=\"display:none\">&amp;#xfeff; / &lt;span class=\"geo\">33.72972; -78.84333&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/span>]&lt;/span>[[Category:Pages using gadget WikiMiniAtlas]]&lt;/span>"}}'/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Coordinates_on_Wikidata"/></td></tr><tr><th scope="row" class="infobox-label" style="font-weight:bold; border: 0;">Area</th><td class="infobox-data" style="border: 0;">164.8 acres (66.7<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>ha)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row" class="infobox-label" style="font-weight:bold; border: 0;">Built</th><td class="infobox-data" style="border: 0;">1926</td></tr><tr><th scope="row" class="infobox-label" style="font-weight:bold; border: 0;">Architects</th><td class="infobox-data" style="border: 0;">Hood, Raymond; White, Robert</td></tr><tr><th scope="row" class="infobox-label" style="font-weight:bold; border: 0;">Architectural<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>style</th><td class="infobox-data" style="border: 0;">Classical Revival</td></tr><tr><th scope="row" class="infobox-label" style="font-weight:bold; border: 0;"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Multiple_Property_Submission" title="Multiple Property Submission" class="mw-redirect">MPS</a></th><td class="infobox-data" style="border: 0;"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://npgallery.nps.gov/NRHP/GetAsset/NRHP/64500568_text" class="external text">Myrtle Beach MPS</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row" class="infobox-label" style="font-weight:bold; border: 0;">NRHP<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>reference<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span><abbr title="number" about="#mwt18" typeof="mw:ExpandedAttrs" data-mw='{"attribs":[[{"txt":"title"},{"html":"&lt;span typeof=\"mw:Nowiki\" id=\"mwCg\">number&lt;/span>"}]]}'>No.</abbr></th><td class="infobox-data" style="border: 0;"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://npgallery.nps.gov/AssetDetail/NRIS/96001219" class="external text">96001219</a><sup about="#mwt15" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-nris_1-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"nris"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-nris-1"}}'><a href="#cite_note-nris-1" id="mwCw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDQ">[</span>1<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDg">]</span></span></a></sup></td></tr><tr><th scope="row" class="infobox-label" style="font-weight:bold; border: 0;">Added to NRHP</th><td class="infobox-data" style="border: 0;">November 7, 1996</td></tr></tbody></table>
+<p id="mwDw"><b id="mwEA">Ocean Forest Country Club</b>, previously known as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ocean_Forest_Hotel" title="Ocean Forest Hotel" id="mwEQ">Ocean Forest Hotel</a> and Country Club,<sup about="#mwt21" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-natregister_2-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"natregister"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-natregister-2"}}'><a href="#cite_note-natregister-2" id="mwEg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFA">[</span>2<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFQ">]</span></span></a></sup> and called <b id="mwFg">Pine Lakes Country Club</b> since 1946,<sup about="#mwt24" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-3"}}'><a href="#cite_note-3" id="mwFw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwGA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwGQ">[</span>3<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwGg">]</span></span></a></sup> is a historic <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Country_club" title="Country club" id="mwGw">country club</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hotel" title="Hotel" id="mwHA">hotel</a> located at <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Myrtle_Beach,_South_Carolina" title="Myrtle Beach, South Carolina" id="mwHQ">Myrtle Beach</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Horry_County,_South_Carolina" title="Horry County, South Carolina" id="mwHg">Horry County, South Carolina</a>.<sup about="#mwt27" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-nrhpinv_4-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"nrhpinv"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-nrhpinv-4"}}'><a href="#cite_note-nrhpinv-4" id="mwHw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwIA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwIQ">[</span>4<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwIg">]</span></span></a></sup> The club and hotel were designed by an influential New York architect, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raymond_Hood" title="Raymond Hood" id="mwIw">Raymond Hood</a> (1881-1934) and is an unusual example of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neoclassical_architecture" title="Neoclassical architecture" id="mwJA">Classical Revival</a> architecture. Construction of the club began in 1926 and was completed in 1927. In addition to the hotel / club building, a 27-hole <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Golf_course" title="Golf course" id="mwJQ">golf course</a> was built in association with the club.  It was designed by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robert_W._White_(golfer)" title="Robert W. White (golfer)" id="mwJg">Robert White</a>, a golf course designer and future president of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Professional_Golfers'_Association_of_America" title="Professional Golfers' Association of America" id="mwJw">Professional Golfers' Association of America</a>. The present 18-hole course dates to 1946.<sup about="#mwt30" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-scdah_5-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"scdah"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-scdah-5"}}'><a href="#cite_note-scdah-5" id="mwKA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwKQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKg">[</span>5<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>
+
+<p id="mwLA">It was listed on the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Register_of_Historic_Places" title="National Register of Historic Places" id="mwLQ">National Register of Historic Places</a> in 1996.<sup about="#mwt31" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-nris_1-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"nris"}}'><a href="#cite_note-nris-1" id="mwLg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwMA">[</span>1<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwMQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>
